### 4.2.2 Reaction-network reduction at fixed species count (522 -> 415 reactions)

The same validation-driven greedy loop was then applied to the *reaction network* of the 69-species
member (`results/red59_bA.yaml`, 522 reactions), on the same 77-case ignition probe with a wider
tolerance box (mean 0.15 / p95 0.35 / max 0.90).  The container job
(`job_c6e4f010d3b0d763c79fed74`) accepted 15 batches and stopped at its own wall-clock deadline
(2077 s of 2100 s) at **69 species / 415 reactions** - a further 20 % of the reaction network -
with probe mean |dln tau| = 0.107, p95 = 0.350, max = 0.504, 0 failed cases.

Held-out validation of that file (`results/rxn_final_r1.yaml`, container job
`job_048fa2cec74a04f879f32b02`, same drivers as everything else):

| observable | 69 sp / 522 rxn (delivered) | 69 sp / 415 rxn (attempt) |
|---|---|---|
| ignition, 792 held-out cases: mean / p95 / max \|dln tau\| | 0.060 / 0.233 / 0.359 | 0.092 / 0.281 / 0.659 |
| ignition, fraction of cases > 35 % | 1.1 % | 3.8 % |
| flame, 11 fuels, phi = 1, 300 K, 1 atm: mean / worst \|dSu/Su\| | 2.9 % / 11.5 % | 14.3 % / 25.6 % |
| flame, sign of the deviation | mixed (+1.4 % ... -11.5 %) | all fuels low (-2.9 % ... -25.6 %, CH3OH worst) |
| element balance / T_ad_HP vs parent | clean / identical | clean / identical |

A further 20 % cut of the reaction network - accepted by the ignition box - costs a factor ~1.5 in
mean ignition error and a factor ~5 in mean flame error, and the flame deficit is *systematic*
(every fuel is slow) rather than a single bad case.  The file is kept as an audit-trail artefact and
is **not delivered** (section 6, item 17).  Two honest caveats: the run stopped at its deadline
rather than at saturation, so a smaller reduction (the first accepted batches were 512 / 486 / 470
reactions, with probe means 0.056 / 0.083 / 0.091) may well sit closer to the parent on flames - but
those intermediate mechanisms were not declared as job outputs and were not archived, so they cannot
be examined without re-running the stage; and the reaction tolerance box, like the species box, is
ignition-only (section 5, limitation 2).

**Flame-protected reaction reduction (a direct test of that headroom).**  We repeated the reaction
stage with a protection rule - reactions containing any species of the core radical pool may never
be removed (`--protect-rxns`, added to `scripts/reduce_engine.py` for this test; container job
`job_b7058a0c1d1183be09759cf2`, tight box mean 0.10 / p95 0.25 / max 0.60, `remote/run_reduce.py`
wrapper):

| variant | protected species | eligible | accepted | final | held-out ignition mean / p95 / max (> 35 %) | flame, 11 fuels: mean / max | worst fuel |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A | 14 core-pool species | 27 / 522 | 6 | 497 rxn | 0.080 / 0.259 / 0.834 (2.9 %) | 5.0 % / 12.1 % | C6H6 -12.1 % |
| B | 8 small radicals | 46 / 522 | 9 | 482 rxn | 0.079 / 0.252 / 0.837 (2.9 %) | 5.1 % / 13.0 % | C6H6 -13.0 % |
| (reference) unconstrained 4.2.2 run | none | 522 | 15 | 415 rxn | 0.092 / 0.281 / 0.659 (3.8 %) | 14.3 % / 25.6 % | CH3OH -25.6 % |
| (delivered) 522-reaction member | - | - | - | 522 rxn | 0.060 / 0.233 / 0.359 (1.1 %) | 2.9 % / 11.5 % | C3H6 -11.5 % |

The marginal cost of reaction removal is steep and does not vanish under protection: taking away
the 25 reactions that do *not* touch the core pool already doubles the mean flame error (2.9 % ->
5.0 %), and taking away 40 costs the same 2 points more.  For comparison, cutting six *species*
(69 -> 63) at 461 reactions costs only +1.2 points (4.1 %).  Both protected variants are also
dominated by the delivered 63-species member, which has fewer species (63), fewer reactions (461)
and a smaller flame error - so neither is delivered; the experiment's value is the quantitative
statement that at fixed species the reaction network of this mechanism has essentially no
flame-neutral headroom left, whereas the delivered members' reaction counts are already the
parent's own steps.

**How much reaction-network headroom is there at all?**  Counting, in the 522-reaction member,
the reactions that contain at least one species of a protected set (computed locally with
`kinlib.reaction_species_sets`):

| protected set | reactions containing it | reactions still eligible for removal |
|---|---|---|
| core radical pool, 14 species (H, O, OH, HO2, H2O2, HCO, CH2O, CH3, CH2, CH, CO, CO2, CH2OH, CH3O) | 495 / 522 | 27 (5.2 %) |
| core pool + C1-C2, 20 species | 507 / 522 | 15 (2.9 %) |
| only the ten species that the flame-informed back-add restored | 126 / 522 | 396 (75.9 %) |

So at fixed species count the reaction network is *almost entirely* core-pool chemistry: any
flame-safe reduction can only touch a few per cent of it, whereas the unconstrained ignition-box
stage was happy to delete 20 % (with the 14 % flame penalty documented above).  The last row also
shows why the repair worked: the ten back-added species appear in only a quarter of the reactions -
the collapse was caused by deleting *species*, not by deleting most reactions.

### 4.2.3 Diagnosing and repairing the lean-propene defect of the compact members (six-species repair)

Section 4.2.1's lean corner exposed a large error of the two compact members (-22.6 % at 1 atm,
-28.7 % at 5 atm on phi = 0.7 propene at 300 K) while the 93-species member stays within 1 %.  The
members had lost the allyl / propenyl-aldehyde branch of the parent (CH3CCH2, CH3CHCH,
CH3CHOCH2, CH3CHCHCHO, C2H3CHO, iC4H5 and their reactions): exactly the chemistry a lean propene
flame is sensitive to, and exactly the chemistry the high-temperature ignition probe does *not*
flag - re-adding it moves the 792-case ignition statistics by less than the tolerance box
(0.108 vs 0.111 mean error against the 63-species member).
Two repair candidates were therefore built by re-adding parent species to the 63-species member
(`scripts/mk_backadd.py`), with no rates or thermo touched:

* `results/red50_bA_p2.yaml` = 63 sp + {CH3CCH2, CH3CHCH} = **65 sp / 493 rxn**
* `results/red50_bA_p6.yaml` = 63 sp + {CH3CCH2, CH3CHCH, CH3CHOCH2, CH3CHCHCHO, C2H3CHO, iC4H5} = **69 sp / 517 rxn**

